Base: signed 381d3fd141eaecae3ea740b363d95fb4e6a9c4e9. Work remains isolated
in bboxy450-log-converter-p1; no merge, release or base-clone changes.

Implemented final contract:
- src/ir/mod.rs:43/51/55 — EventId is the first 16 bytes of BLAKE3 over exactly
  five UTF-8 frames: bxl.event.v1, provider, native_id, native_key and role_tag.
  Every frame, including domain and empty role, is u32 BE length plus bytes.
  Native role is empty. Inferred boundaries use unchanged anchor native_key and
  the separate turn-start / turn-end role; no # suffix is appended to the key.
- tests/cbor_compat.rs:212/274 — fixed vectors, and a deliberate unframed control
  that collides across s1/23 and s12/3. First-16-byte vectors for Claude:
    synthetic / uuid-0 / empty:      c9a0c026c023e33f268e8f015fe98bf0
    synthetic / uuid-0 / turn-start: 2de168098b1152958111559ca5a86dd8
    synthetic / uuid-0 / turn-end:   cbea0ffaeea0e690767d9b931ee03c4d
    s1 / 23 / empty:                e34f3349414f162f5e50655ad645db33
    s12 / 3 / empty:                4b7981a5040f1f504c42b12d133e9189
  An independent literal-preimage helper pins these against the locked BLAKE3
  dependency; none is assembled by EventId::native inside the vector helper.
- tests/cbor_compat.rs:326/336 and tests/cbor_golden.rs:237/241 — the fixed mixed
  key set is exactly {10,23,24,100,-1,"a"}. Canonical order: 10,23,24,100,-1,"a".
  Six-entry map with null values, fixed golden bytes:
    a60af617f61818f61864f620f66161f6
  The length-first broken writer emits 10,23,-1,24,100,"a":
    a60af617f620f61818f61864f66161f6
  The control explicitly fails the same fixed-byte comparison.
- tests/cbor_compat.rs:405 — valid noncanonical input is accepted: reversed map
  order; indefinite maps/arrays/text/bytes; nonpreferred integer, tag and float
  widths. Re-emission equals canonical fixtures, including the mixed-key record.
  Existing duplicate/malformed/trailing-record rejection remains enforced.
- tests/fixtures/ir-v0.1.hex deliberately regenerated again for the final five-
  field identity contract and prescribed mixed-key set. Still 68 cases; 65 byte
  vectors changed. Two Session vectors and the minimal Event stay unchanged.
  The ordinary golden test never rewrites fixtures; the one-use generator was
  removed. No production CBOR comparator change was needed after the prior fix.
- README.md and verification/README.md document the final source pin, framing,
  exact mixed-key control and permissive-reader/canonical-writer split. The P2
  typed extension-editing advisory remains recorded, without scope expansion.

